@@ -70,6 +70,14 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. It does not pretty print, wrap, crop, apply markup, or replace emoji codes, so the text is written exactly as given. It does apply highlighting (enabled by default, with ``highlight=None`` deferring to the console setting) and an optional basic ``style``.
+
+    >>> console.out("[bold]Hello[/bold]", "World :smile:")
+
+
